{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013898-i-ve-got-a-game-plan","id":1013898,"title":"I've got a Game Plan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-07T12:18:46-08:00","id":1013898,"title":"I've got a Game Plan","content":"On the chance that anyone might be interested, I thought I might share the bits and pieces I'm putting together for an upcoming game. I've got me some players, I've got me some thoughts, and I think I've got me a workable premise.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Unthank Chronicle: Living a Weird Shit Life</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>&quot;Say, Rose? Do you believe in Magic?&quot; </i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>&quot;Not really, no. But that's not what you're asking me.&quot; </i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>&quot;It's not?&quot; </i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>&quot;Nope. What you're asking me is, do I believe in weird shit? And the answer is yes. Of course I do. I'd be crazy not to. I've had a weird shit life.&quot;</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Rose and Carla, The Sandman: The Kindly Ones</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After far, </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>far</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, too long without a face-to-face tabletop game I\u2019m giving in and trying something new. By the glory of teh intarwebs whall a game be assembled via remote communication, and by scavenging from a dozen different half-finished campaign ideas for far too many systems shall a plot be assembled.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Given that starting a game in mid-December is surest folly, I\u2019m aiming for a January start.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unthank, where we lay our scene, is a fictitious city-state on a peninsula off of the east coast of Panama. A hub for finance and shipping, legitimate and otherwise, it also has a reputation as a sinkhole for eccentrics and strange goings on. For nearly a century the Mages of the Pentacle Orders have been shut out of Unthank by the sworn word of a respected master, but with his passing it has been decided that a group of initiates of promising potential should be the first representatives to reestablish contact. The mission is not for the faint of heart, but the potential rewards are not to be sniffed at.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, gather your grimoires and draw up some pentagrams. It\u2019s time to pretend you\u2019re a wizard.</span><br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Themes and Conceits</span></u></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh Brave New World, That Has Such Monsters In It</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is an explicitly alternate timeline and setting for this game, along with a world in which even the most resolute muggle brushes against the strange on occasion \u2013 even if everything from their own memory to the world itself contrives to make them think otherwise.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Mysterium is right, then the living fabric of sorcery hides mysteries from those who seek it, per a quality they name Pancryptia. If they aren\u2019t right, the strangest parts of the world seem to settle out of sight and that\u2019s just the way it is.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unthank in particular is home to a disproportionate share of the universe\u2019s Misc Drawer. On one hand this presents an opportunity for Mages to explore a city where the strange is a little closer to the surface, on the other it is a chance for the ST to indulge in the weirder and more obscure entities and effects from the Chronicles of Darkness / New World of Darkness books.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Addicted to Mystery, Prone to Obsession, Flypaper for the Strange</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike Vampires, Werewolves and the other player character types, Mages have nothing concrete which functions as a stop on a normal life. There is no soul-deep thirst for blood or simmering spiritual frenzy stopping a Willworker packing away their magic wand and fancy robes to live a normal life, and indeed most of the powers that be would be more than happy to have one less active troublemaker picking at the seams of reality. The problem is, that doesn\u2019t happen.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is not one Mage who can leave well enough alone. An inquisitive nature is all but required to Awaken in the first instance, and the experience does nothing to quell the thirst for understanding. Even when the lure of a normal life takes them away from combing the streets for their next anomaly, their very nature tends to draw oddities to them as the subtlest of magics swirl around them, inviting them back into the search.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You Don\u2019t Have to be Mad to Work Here, but it Helps</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The process of Awakening shifts your perspective on life, the universe and everything to a place out of sync with the norm, but even the norm can be pretty abnormal. Mages are disproportionately drawn from society\u2019s fringes and those who have had run-ins with magics from an outside perspective. Consider how much this applied to your character when building them. Odd cults, obsessions with conspiracy theories, time spent in amongst ghost-haunted ruins or as a member of a cell of monster hunters are all entirely suitable. A certain level of Special and Unique Snowflake is expected.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the same time, however, moderation is advised. Spending your childhood convinced your dead brother is trying to talk to you only to be proven right is entirely appropriate; being raised by a temple of mystic martial artists is stretching it, but could work with some effort and some subversion of expectations. The last survivor of an alternate timeline or the Chosen Child of a magical bloodline are more likely to come across as silly than anything else.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nothing Worth Having Comes Easy</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unthank has been without a proper presence amongst the Pentacle Orders for nearly a century, but that only means that those who would normally have to fight for the reigns and places of power have been down one set of opponents. Progress requires either finding new knowledge (and there\u2019s always reasons it\u2019s still hidden), taking it by force (and they won\u2019t give up easy), or negotiating for access (and you\u2019ll get bog-all without something worth trading) - good luck.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What\u2019s Yours is Mine and What\u2019s Mine is My Own</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Obviously, the Convocations and Masters who are sponsoring this expedition want the Pentacle Orders to profit from this untapped source of knowledge \u2013 after all, this is a joint undertaking in the spirit of cooperation. Equally obviously, all of them want to profit more than their competitors \u2013 after all, you don\u2019t advance amongst your peers by giving away </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>all</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> your secrets.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They player characters will have to embrace this contradiction \u2013 one-upmanship and posturing for position are needed if they don\u2019t want to become sidelined irrelevancies, but if they don\u2019t work together effectively then nobody wins.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Character Creation</span></u></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Who Are These Weirdos, and Why Are They Here? </span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For nearly a century the Pentacle Orders have been all but unknown in Unthank, bound by the oath of one of the Arrow\u2019s most respected Acanthus Masters. However, this is about to change.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Players\u2019 Cabal are the chosen representatives of the Pentacle. They may be precocious young prodigies given a chance for glory, or they may be troublemakers being sent on a dangerous mission half way across the world - either way, they have plenty of motivation to make the best of things.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If possible, both to maximise niche protection and to allow for the ever-fun conflicting ideologies, The ST would like to see at least one player from each Pentacle order (Adamantine Arrow; Guardians of the Veil; Mysterium; Silver Ladder and Free Council) and from each Path (Acanthus, Mastigos, Moros, Obrimos and Thyrsus). If the initial interest numbers hold true, this should not be difficult.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seers of the Throne, Banishers, and the various other nogoodniks are reserved for NPCs.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mechanics</span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Player characters are created using the rules starting on p79 of Mage the Awakening Second Edition. These Mages have gotten a grip on their new lives, but have a way to go before becoming movers and shakers.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to this, characters get a few points added by the wise and benevolent ST, representing extra training and/or support from the Orders who sent them. This will be added after character creation is complete.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Building Your Character</span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>All characters are new to Unthank, making certain merits (such as Safe Place, local Contacts and Allies and Hallow) problematic or completely unviable. Any mundane connections and sites are limited to those that a character has built up remotely or via friends of friends. Magical connections and places of power are not allowed at startup.</li> <li>The Profession merit is extremely cost effective, and worth looking at. However, it also requires a significant amount of investment for the character. By the very fact that you have upped sticks to move to a new country, your professional life has been disrupted, and you will be hard pressed to justify more than two or perhaps three dots.<ul><li>As a corollary to the above, for those characters whose supernal lives have blossomed at the expense of the mundane, \u201cConcillium Enforcer\u201d, \u201cWeird Librarian\u201d and \u201cGoddamn Wizard\u201d are all valid choices. However, a magical career will have if anything been upended even more than more normal ones.</li> </ul></li> <li>The official and working language of Unthank is English. Spanish is also common, with most road signs and advertising being bilingual. Zoar Creole is spoken on the peninsula, as is Cab\u00e9ku (a native language of the Chibchan family).</li> <li>XP costs are (as of 2nd edition) flat - making optimisation at character creation less of a Thing. The ST will not be expecting characters engineered to the finest tolerances, and expects to be fairly generous with advancement.</li> <li>When creating Aspirations, remember that these are what the player wants to have happen to their character, not necessarily what the character wants. A parade of choices between awful options or being broken by torture are just as valid as a desire to gain great wealth or reconcile with your mentor.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:02:54-08:00","id":1015760,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify: is this a recruitment thread for your game, or just a place for feedback and possibly posting APs once you get started?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:47:23-08:00","id":1016121,"title":"","content":"Feedback and general interest. I had a scour at just about everything I could find of a similar nature on teh intarwebs, and figured it might be passingly interesting to post up my own.<br /> <br /> Apologies for my apparent inability to be clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}